0","event_uuid":"469e74e2-70be-431c-ba87-5caaba1c175f","position":{"commit_sha":"8883dd47a0e250e7937bfe15198c371f99d2cd11","position":"1786571125502983001-469e74e2-70be-431c-ba87-5caaba1c175f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"43677055f116cea8455e10eb8c4ffb8974be0dd28d55816159feb2a19897f3e2","event_uuid":"e829440f-00e7-4150-ba22-fbc2cfaeea42","position":{"commit_sha":"53a1b4da9f11601dd7e44d5f2d1e7a1f6b45ef5b","position":"1786571669455871884-e829440f-00e7-4150-ba22-fbc2cfaeea42"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786558471405692001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7b175128-c312-430c-babb-fb9b02f58b4d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"248f-ac00-18db-4259"},{"link_uuid":"e829440f-00e7-4150-ba22-fbc2cfaeea42","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5e05-7392-68b4-4f54"}],"description":"## Context\n\nParent epic `a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb`; depends on S1 (`248f-ac00-18db-4259`), which adds the\npeer-confirmation store and records a confirmation when WE push a link. This story adds the\nsecond, independent evidence source: a link observed in an authoritative remote snapshot is\npeer-confirmed even if this clone never pushed it (peer-created links, links pushed before the\nstore existed, links pushed by another clone).\n\nThe epic's binding constraint: **a partial / paginated / failed / stale read is NON-EVIDENCE** —\nit can neither confirm nor deny. rebar already has exactly this completeness signal, and this\nstory consumes it rather than inventing one. `fetcher.py::merge_issuelinks_map` writes the\nper-issue `issuelinks` key ONLY on an authoritative read — an absent key means UNOBSERVED\n(truncated page walk, HTTP 410, failed enrichment, a backend without `get_issuelinks_map`),\nwhile `[]` means authoritatively-empty. This is the same G1 signal the inbound removal differ\nalready depends on. `BackendPaginationStallError` re-raises rather than degrading, so a stalled\npager never reaches this code as a complete read.\n\nThere is no snapshot revision counter in the codebase; `pass_id` is the only handle (epic\ncomment D3), so records store `confirmed_pass`, not an ordered revision. No ordering logic is\nbuilt on it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `peer_confirmations.py` — add\n  `confirm_from_snapshot(store, curr_snapshot, binding_store, pass_id) -> int`, returning the\n  number of records written.\n  - Iterate `curr_snapshot` entries. **Process an entry ONLY if `\"issuelinks\" in entry`** — an\n    absent key is UNOBSERVED and must be skipped whole. Use the `in` test, never\n    `entry.get(\"issuelinks\") or []`, which collapses observed-empty into unobserved (the exact\n    trap `inbound_differ.py`'s G1 docstring warns about).\n  - Source local id is `binding_store.get_local_id(jira_key)`; skip the entry when it is None.\n  - For each raw link entry use `link_direction.resolve_inbound_link(link)` to get\n    `(other_key, relation)` in LOCAL relation vocabulary, then\n    `binding_store.get_local_id(other_key)` for the target. Skip entries where either is None.\n    `resolve_inbound_link` is used directly rather than `observed_peer_deps` because the latter\n    returns only `(relation, target)` and DISCARDS the vendor link id this story must persist.\n  - Record each as `direction=\"snapshot\"`, `source=\"snapshot\"`, `link_id=link.get(\"id\")`,\n    `confirmed_pass=pass_id`.\n- `reconcile.py::_persist_and_log` — call it inside the existing `if persist:` block, as a\n  sibling of the `_advance_baselines(binding_store, ctx.curr_snapshot, ctx.synced_fields)` call\n  and BEFORE `binding_store.save()`, wrapped in the same fail-open `try/except Exception` shape\n  that call already uses (log to stderr, never break a sync pass). Then `store.save()`.\n- Confirmation is monotonic and additive: observing a link confirms it; NOT observing it never\n  un-confirms. Un-confirmation is deliberately excluded — it would reintroduce \"absence is\n  evidence\", the exact failure the epic forbids.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A snapshot entry with `issuelinks` present and a bound link produces a record with\n      `direction=\"snapshot\"`, `source=\"snapshot\"`, `link_id` from the raw entry's `id`, and the\n      current `pass_id`. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py -k observed`.\n- [ ] AC2 A snapshot entry with the `issuelinks` key ABSENT produces NO record for that issue,\n      even when the link is present and managed locally. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py -k unobserved`.\n- [ ] AC3 An authoritative `issuelinks: []` produces no record and does NOT remove or invalidate\n      an existing confirmation. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py -k empty_authoritative`.\n- [ ] AC4 A link whose source or target key is unbound is skipped — no record, no raise. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py -k unbound`.\n- [ ] AC5 Relation mapping goes through `link_direction`, so an INWARD `Blocks` entry is recorded\n      under `depends_on`, not `blocks`. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py -k direction`.\n- [ ] AC6 An exception raised inside snapshot confirmation is logged and the reconcile pass still\n      completes and persists (injected raising store). Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py -k fail_open`.\n- [ ] AC7 In no-write mode (`persist` False) no confirmation is written. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py -k nowrite`.\n- [ ] AC8 Every edited module stays under the 800-line cap. Proof: `bash -c 'git archive HEAD |\n      tar -xO src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py | wc -l'` per edited file, < 800.\n- [ ] AC9 Gates green. Proof: `make lint` exit 0, `make typecheck` exit 0,\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` exit 0.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New suite `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py` covering the\n  observed / unobserved / authoritative-empty trichotomy, unbound source and target, inward\n  direction mapping, fail-open behavior, and the no-write path.\n- Regression: `make lint && make typecheck && pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` — this story is\n  additive and must not change any differ or apply behavior.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe removal decline (S3) and the upgrade backfill (S4). No un-confirmation. No new fetch — this\nstory consumes `ctx.curr_snapshot` as already fetched.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py","reason":"add confirm_from_snapshot (completeness-aware)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"call snapshot confirmation in the persist phase beside _advance_baselines"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py","reason":"NEW: observed/unobserved/empty-authoritative and direction-mapping cases"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","248f-ac00-18db-4259"],["parent","a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb"],["relates_to","5e05-7392-68b4-4f54"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb","parent_status_uuid":"c0ddaf77-8fa7-4c7f-bd65-61cb3baf8792","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"83d3-61d9-fc59-424b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Confirm links from authoritative fetched snapshots","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ab80febf-6e14-498a-8322-21d64b4f8b20","5e1c0f81-d949-4b83-be4e-d3d2d26f326a","7b175128-c312-430c-babb-fb9b02f58b4d","7b1473d3-b833-486f-ac70-c6796d4375d9","854778db-4517-4a41-a2a5-68b97fa009c3","c0ddaf77-8fa7-4c7f-bd65-61cb3baf8792","469e74e2-70be-431c-ba87-5caaba1c175f","e829440f-00e7-4150-ba22-fbc2cfaeea42"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786571669455871885,"uuid":"58ed9fe6-821e-4f49-b7f6-8dfb9734454e"}